"""Small source-backed notebook of promising next inputs and actual availability."""
import json,os
import nbformat
from scripts.audit_next_predictor_sources import OUT
from scripts.build_supervisor_model_review import execute,export_html


def main():
    audit=json.loads((OUT/'internal_availability.json').read_text())
    food=json.loads((OUT/'historical_food_api_probe.json').read_text())
    candidates=[
      {'Input':'Pest counts and improvement from visit 1 to 3','Why test it':'Direct evidence that infestation persisted or declined','Data found':'0 named pest-count fields; 0 named severity fields in 5,598 archived services','Next step':'Needs real dated inspection/trap records; do not invent a severity score'},
      {'Input':'Actual product, dose, treatment and access problems','Why test it':'May explain incomplete coverage or an unsuitable treatment','Data found':'10 named method fields (8 pass snapshot timing gate); no named dose or access fields','Next step':'Mostly new collection; appointment method is not completed treatment'},
      {'Input':'Calendar team and continuity between visits','Why test it':'Possible service-process signal; also affected by routes and property mix','Data found':'All 10,690 archived Calendar events have calendar names','Next step':'Match service IDs and as-of snapshots; team is not an individual technician'},
      {'Input':'Booked visit length, property type and size','Why test it':'Context about service complexity and planned effort','Data found':'10,659 raw events have positive scheduled length; 4 named size fields; no named property-type field','Next step':'Booked time is not actual work; validate property type extraction and event joins'},
      {'Input':'Recent returns involving the same pest at the property or nearby','Why test it':'More specific recent history than combining every pest together','Data found':'Pest category, service dates, prior returns and geocoded locations already exist','Next step':'Derive past-only pest-specific rates; existing general history is already in the model'},
      {'Input':'Historically mapped nearby food places','Why test it':'Potential local food-source/land-use context','Data found':'Historical public API probe succeeded for 2024, 2025 and 2026','Next step':'Collect buffered counts as of each service date; check duplicate POIs and mapping coverage'},
      {'Input':'Building age','Why test it':'Possible proxy for maintenance and entry-point conditions','Data found':'Earlier 100-location audit found 0 verified construction ages; no named age field in archive','Next step':'Needs verified developer/owner construction year and exact building match'}]
    md=nbformat.v4.new_markdown_cell;code=nbformat.v4.new_code_cell
    nb=nbformat.v4.new_notebook(cells=[
      md('# Which new inputs are worth testing?\n\n**There are useful leads, but none has demonstrated a performance improvement yet.** The most direct inputs—pest counts, improvement after treatment, actual product/dose and access conditions—are largely missing from the records checked.\n\nTwo practical next directions are richer pest-specific historical features and historical food-place context. Calendar team/continuity and booked duration are also available candidates after correct source linking. No existing model or test result was changed.'),
      code('import pandas as pd\n'+f'candidates={candidates!r}\n'+"display(pd.DataFrame(candidates))"),
      md('## What was actually checked\n\nThe description audit covers 5,598 archived service windows exported on 27 September 2026. Named fields were checked conservatively in both English and Malay. No detected field does not prove that no information exists elsewhere in free text. A further keyword check found only three severity hints in named Problem/Remark/Note text, and only two passed the snapshot timing gate. Those are not reliable severity labels.\n\nThere are 5,321 named Problem fields, including 4,817 whose snapshot timing passes the historical proxy. Basic pest mentions were already explored in an earlier description-feature experiment; they are not a newly discovered feature. The structured observation template has zero observation records.\n\nThe Calendar schema audit covers a different archived export of 10,690 raw events, including non-service events. Its coverage figures do not establish matching coverage on the model cohort. Event identity and version/timestamp checks are required before use. This was not a fresh read of every live Sheet.'),
      md('## New external source that worked\n\nA bounded public Shah Alam map sample returned historical mapped food-place counts of 9 in January 2024, 13 in January 2025 and 13 in January 2026. The probe counted restaurant/cafe/fast-food/food-court nodes; it was not a complete business census and did not send a customer address.\n\nHistorical map state avoids treating newly mapped places as if they were already known in 2024. It still does not prove when a business opened or closed. Mapping omissions, duplicates, area precision and historical observation dates must remain visible.\n\nThe successful probe used ohsome v1. Its official documentation says v1 retires on 30 November 2026 and v2 requires an API key. A durable integration would need v2 setup; no account was created or purchase made.'),
      code(f"food_samples={food.get('response',{}).get('result',[])!r}\n"+"display(pd.DataFrame(food_samples).rename(columns={'timestamp':'Historical map date','value':'Mapped food nodes in sample box'}))"),
      md('## Why these candidates\n\nUC Integrated Pest Management guidance describes monitoring with traps, sanitation, food/water removal, exclusion and suitable control methods as relevant to cockroach management. EPA guidance similarly emphasizes monitoring and site conditions. This supports our choice of hypotheses; it is not evidence that these fields will improve this company’s model.\n\n[UC IPM cockroach guidance](https://ipm.ucanr.edu/home-and-landscape/cockroaches/)\n\n[EPA integrated pest management principles](https://www.epa.gov/safepestcontrol/integrated-pest-management-ipm-principles)\n\n[ohsome historical API documentation](https://docs.ohsome.org/ohsome-api/v2/)\n\n[ohsome migration and access requirements](https://docs.ohsome.org/ohsome-api/v2/migration_guide.html)'),
      md('## Recommended order\n\n1. Check pest-specific past-return rates, team continuity and valid booked-duration features using aligned service identities and snapshots. Missing values remain unknown.\n2. Collect historical food-place counts around locations with adequate precision. Test them as mapped-context features, not confirmed operating-business counts.\n3. Recover real dated inspection reports if available. Otherwise start collecting pest counts, method/product and access/condition evidence for future research. The present templates cannot supply missing historical facts.\n\nThe latest 2,075-service evaluation is now an assessment set that has been inspected. Do not repeatedly tune new variables against it and claim an untouched final score. Use earlier chronological selection periods for candidate work and keep the real prospective test unchanged.\n\nThe notebook contains aggregate evidence only. Cells were executed sequentially in Python and validated with nbformat; a native Jupyter kernel was unavailable for a second execution check.')])
    previous=os.getcwd()
    try:os.chdir(OUT);execute(nb)
    finally:os.chdir(previous)
    nb.metadata.kernelspec={'display_name':'Python 3','language':'python','name':'python3'}
    for cell in nb.cells:
        if cell.cell_type=='code':cell.metadata['jupyter']={'source_hidden':True}
    nbformat.validate(nb);nbformat.write(nb,OUT/'Next_Useful_Inputs.ipynb');export_html(nb,OUT/'Next_Useful_Inputs.html')
    print('Saved availability review notebook and HTML; no predictor model trained')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
